    {
      "id": "49e5d8b846a7-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "Which of the following is the correct order of basicity? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;? &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is the correct order of basicity?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><b>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:</b></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "LiOH > NaOH > KOH > CsOH LiOH > NaOH > KOH > CsOH",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">LiOH &gt; NaOH &gt; KOH &gt; CsOH</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">LiOH > NaOH > KOH > CsOH</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "LiOH > KOH > CsOH > NaOH LiOH > KOH > CsOH > NaOH",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">LiOH &gt; KOH &gt; CsOH &gt; NaOH</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">LiOH > KOH > CsOH > NaOH</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "KOH > CsOH > NaOH > LiOH KOH > CsOH > NaOH > LiOH",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">KOH &gt; CsOH &gt; NaOH &gt; LiOH</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">KOH > CsOH > NaOH > LiOH</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "CsOH > KOH > NaOH > LiOH CsOH > KOH > NaOH > LiOH",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">CsOH &gt; KOH &gt; NaOH &gt; LiOH</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">CsOH > KOH > NaOH > LiOH</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>1) <b>Definition of Basicity:</b></p><p>o Basicity refers to the strength of a base, which depends on its ability to donate hydroxide ions (OH&#8722;OH^-OH&#8722;) in an aqueous solution.</p><p>2) <b>Trend in Alkali Metal Hydroxides:</b></p><p>o As we move down Group 1 of the periodic table, the hydroxides of alkali metals become stronger bases due to increased ionic size and solubility in water.</p><p>o Order of basicity: CsOH &gt; KOH &gt; NaOH &gt; LiOH.</p><p><b>Explanation of Incorrect Options:</b></p><p>&#183; Option 1, 2, and 3 list incorrect trends that do not align with the periodic properties of alkali metals.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "49e5d8b846a7-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Which of the following elements is a metalloid? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2313;&#2346;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following elements is a metalloid?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2313;&#2346;&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Iron &#2354;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Iron</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Oxygen &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Oxygen</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Sodium &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Sodium</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Silicon &#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2377;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Silicon</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2377;&#2344;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Silicon is classified as a metalloid because it has properties of both metals and non-metals.</p>",
