      "id": "49e5d8b846a7-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "Which element of group 13 is a soft metal with a low melting point (303K) and is widely used in doping semiconductors and producing solid-state devices such as transistors? &#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; 13 &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2350; &#2327;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; (303K) &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2352;&#2350; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2337;&#2379;&#2346;&#2344;/&#2309;&#2346;&#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2306;&#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2352; &#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360;-&#2309;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2346;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which element of group 13 is a soft metal with a low melting point (303K) and is widely used in doping semiconductors and producing solid-state devices such as transistors?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2370;&#2361; 13 &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2350; &#2327;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; (303K) &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2352;&#2350; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2330;&#2366;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2337;&#2379;&#2346;&#2344;/&#2309;&#2346;&#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2324;&#2352; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2306;&#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2352; &#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360;-&#2309;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2346;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Aluminium &#2319;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Aluminium</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2350;&#2368;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Boron &#2348;&#2379;&#2352;&#2377;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Boron</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2379;&#2352;&#2377;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Thallium &#2341;&#2376;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Thallium</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2341;&#2376;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Gallium &#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Gallium</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2376;&#2354;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><b>Gallium</b>, a soft metal of group 13, has the second lowest melting point (after mercury) and can remain in the liquid phase at a larger range of temperatures than any other substance.</p><p>With a low melting point of 303K, it is widely used in doping semiconductors and producing solid-state devices such as transistors.</p>",
